# Moire

Read `AGENTS.md` before changing renderer, inverse math, or HUD.

- Keep CPU (`inverseCpu.ts`) and WGSL (`inverse.wgsl.ts`) twins. Lattices: `latticeCpu.ts` / `lattice.wgsl.ts`. One `fn` per `wgslFn`.
- Rotation needs an `n` sweep; do not cap rings. Holes at zoom-out are missed sides.
- Do not rebuild `colorNode` when layer count changes. Fixed `MAX_LAYERS` slots. A settled field expression is the only rebuild.
- Fields are expressions compiled to straight-line WGSL (`fields/emit.ts`), never interpreted in the shader. CPU twin is `fields/evalExpr.ts`.
- World Y up; flip Y only in `camera.ts`. `rotation` is degrees, `rotationOffset` is radians.
- One left `Studio` chrome (Jupiter logo, layers, PNG export). `I` collapses it. `E` exports. No separate HUD / inspector / filmstrip, and no `View` section.
- Envelope is a header icon toggle with contrast in a popover on it. Fields are a calligraphic `f` per layer row opening a modal. Active state is fill and colour, never a ring.
- Default background is white. Studio chrome is dark. Lines family icon is `Asterisk02Icon`.
- Studio groups Lines, Concentric, Grid, Curves. Lines: Parallel + Radial. Concentric: Circle, Square, Triangle, Hexagon. Curves: Wave (`Sine02Icon`), Parabola (`Parabola01Icon`), Hyperbola (`HyperboleIcon`), Spiral (`SpiralsIcon`). Family icon is `ShellIcon`.
- Radial lines use `lineCount`, not spacing or offset. Start (`phase`) opens a hole at the origin. Curves: Wave has Amplitude, Frequency, Phase; Parabola opens up (`y = ax²`); Hyperbola is rectangular; Spiral spacing is the arm gap, pitch sets starts. Option-drag rotates around the world origin. Shift on sliders is fine control. Grids stretch with Scale X/Y. First paint shows two default concentric layers, then eases into the preset. Type changes ease on the GPU (~280 ms, distance mix). Do not resurrect `maxRings`, JSON import, or fake blends.
